---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

// Internal notes for whoever edits this file next live here, in the
// frontmatter, because frontmatter never reaches the browser. An HTML comment
// ships in the page source, where any visitor can read it (XFO-96).
//
// How long we keep it. The periods for our own systems were confirmed by the
// business on 11 October 2026 (XFO-47): 24 months from last contact for
// non-customer enquiries and chats, 6 years after the work ends for customer
// records. If either changes, the data protection addendum given to customers
// has to change with it, or the two documents contradict each other.
//
// Website measurement is stated as a criterion rather than a number on
// purpose. A fixed period would be a promise about a PostHog retention setting
// we have not verified we can control on our plan, and a policy that names a
// period we do not enforce is worse than one that names a criterion we do.
---

<BaseLayout
	title="Privacy Policy | XFour"
	description="How XFour IT Limited handles personal data collected through xfour.co.uk: what we collect, why, how long we keep it, and your rights."
>
    <section class="clean-block clean-info dark">
        <div class="container">
            <div class="block-heading">
                <h1 class="text-info">Privacy Policy</h1>
                <p>What we collect through this website, why we are allowed to, how long we keep it, and what you can ask us
                    to do about it.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>
    <section class="clean-block">
        <div class="container">
            <article class="mx-auto" style="max-width: 50rem;">

                <h2 class="h4">Who we are</h2>
                <p>XFour IT Limited, trading as XFour, is the data controller for the personal information described in this
                    policy. We provide Microsoft Dynamics 365 consultancy and managed IT support to small businesses in
                    Reading and across the Thames Valley.</p>
                <ul>
                    <li>Company number 11776254, registered in England and Wales. VAT number GB396767915.</li>
                    <li>Registered office: 100 Berkshire Place, C/O KT Wells Ltd, Winnersh Triangle, Wokingham, RG41 5RD.</li>
                    <li>For anything about your personal information, email
                        <a href="mailto:gdpr@xfour.co.uk">gdpr@xfour.co.uk</a>, or call 0118 370 2920.</li>
                </ul>
                <p>We are not required to appoint a Data Protection Officer. Enquiries to the address above reach the person
                    responsible.</p>

                <h2 class="h4 mt-5">What this policy covers</h2>
                <p>This policy covers <strong>www.xfour.co.uk</strong>: the live chat, our contact details, the booking link,
                    and the measurement we run on the site.</p>
                <p>Two things it does not cover:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>If you become a customer</strong>, your agreement with us includes a data protection addendum
                        that sets out exactly what we hold, for how long and why. That addendum governs the work we do for
                        you, and takes precedence over this policy where the two overlap.</li>
                    <li><strong>Slay</strong>, our iOS app, has its own policy at
                        <a href="/legal/slay">xfour.co.uk/legal/slay</a>, because the app collects nothing and runs no
                        trackers at all.</li>
                </ul>

                <h2 class="h4 mt-5">What we collect, why, and our lawful basis</h2>
                <p>UK GDPR requires us to have a specific legal reason for each use of your information. Here is each one.</p>

                <h3 class="h5 mt-4">1. If you use the live chat</h3>
                <p><strong>What:</strong> the messages you send, anything you choose to tell us in them such as your name,
                    email address, phone number or company, and technical details the chat service needs in order to work.</p>
                <p><strong>Why:</strong> to answer your question and, if you are asking about our services, to follow up.</p>
                <p><strong>Lawful basis:</strong> <em>legitimate interests</em> — replying to someone who has contacted us
                    about our business. Where your question is about taking on our services, our basis is also
                    <em>steps taken at your request before entering a contract</em>. Separately, the cookies and browser
                    storage the chat needs are placed only with your <em>consent</em>, which is what our cookie banner asks
                    for. You can refuse, and the chat simply does not load.</p>
                <p><strong>Where it goes:</strong> the chat is Microsoft Dynamics 365 Omnichannel. The conversation is stored
                    in our own Dynamics 365 system so that we can answer you and find the conversation again later.</p>

                <h3 class="h5 mt-4">2. If you email, call, or book a meeting with us</h3>
                <p><strong>What:</strong> your name, your email address or phone number, and whatever you tell us. If you use
                    our Microsoft Bookings link, Microsoft collects the details you type into the booking form and the
                    appointment itself.</p>
                <p><strong>Why:</strong> to reply, to hold the appointment, and to keep a record of what was agreed.</p>
                <p><strong>Lawful basis:</strong> <em>legitimate interests</em> in responding to an enquiry about our
                    business, and <em>steps taken at your request before entering a contract</em> where you are asking us to
                    quote or to work for you.</p>

                <h3 class="h5 mt-4">3. Measuring how the website is used</h3>
                <p><strong>What:</strong> which pages were opened, in what order, where you arrived from, your approximate
                    location from your network address, your device and browser type, and clicks on our phone, email and
                    booking links. We do not record your screen, we do not run surveys, and we do not build a profile of you.</p>
                <p><strong>Why:</strong> so we can tell which pages bring in work and which do not, and spend our effort on
                    the ones that do.</p>
                <p><strong>Lawful basis:</strong> <em>legitimate interests</em> in understanding and improving our own
                    website. We have weighed this against your privacy and set the tools up so that they store nothing on
                    your device and cannot identify you: our measurement tool runs in a cookieless mode where the identifier
                    is rebuilt from scratch every day, so it cannot follow you across days. Even so, you can object at any
                    time — press <strong>Reject</strong> on the cookie banner, or use <strong>Cookie choices</strong> in the
                    footer of any page, and we stop.</p>
                <p>Full detail of each tool is in our <a href="/legal/cookies">cookie policy</a>.</p>

                <h3 class="h5 mt-4">4. Keeping the site available and secure</h3>
                <p><strong>What:</strong> your network address, your browser type and the requests your browser makes, as
                    processed by Cloudflare, who host and protect this site.</p>
                <p><strong>Why:</strong> to serve the site, to block attacks and automated abuse, and to see whether pages
                    are loading properly.</p>
                <p><strong>Lawful basis:</strong> <em>legitimate interests</em> in keeping our website working and defending
                    it from attack. The cookie Cloudflare's security check uses is strictly necessary, so it does not need
                    your consent.</p>

                <h3 class="h5 mt-4">5. Remembering your cookie choice</h3>
                <p><strong>What:</strong> one cookie recording your answer and the date you gave it. No name, no address, no
                    identifier for you.</p>
                <p><strong>Lawful basis:</strong> this is strictly necessary to do the thing you asked us to do, which is to
                    remember your answer and stop asking. Under <em>UK GDPR</em> our basis is <em>legitimate interests</em> in
                    honouring your choice.</p>

                <h2 class="h4 mt-5">What we never do</h2>
                <ul>
                    <li>We do not sell your personal information, and we do not share it for anyone else's advertising.</li>
                    <li>We run no advertising or marketing trackers on this website.</li>
                    <li>We make no decisions about you by automated means, and we do not profile you.</li>
                    <li>This site is aimed at businesses, not children, and we do not knowingly collect information about
                        children.</li>
                </ul>

                <h2 class="h4 mt-5">Who else handles your information</h2>
                <p>These companies process personal information on our instructions, under a contract, and only for the
                    purpose listed. They are not allowed to use it for their own purposes.</p>
                <div class="x4-cookie-table-wrap">
                    <table class="x4-cookie-table">
                        <caption class="visually-hidden">Processors used by XFour for this website</caption>
                        <thead>
                            <tr>
                                <th scope="col">Company</th>
                                <th scope="col">What they do for us</th>
                                <th scope="col">Where it is processed</th>
                            </tr>
                        </thead>
                        <tbody>
                            <tr>
                                <td>Microsoft</td>
                                <td>Runs the live chat, holds our Dynamics 365 records, provides our email and the Bookings
                                    appointment link</td>
                                <td>United Kingdom</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td>PostHog</td>
                                <td>Counts visits and link clicks on this website</td>
                                <td>European Union</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td>Cloudflare</td>
                                <td>Hosts and protects the website, and reports page performance</td>
                                <td>Global network, including the United Kingdom</td>
                            </tr>
                        </tbody>
                    </table>
                </div>
                <p>We will also disclose information if the law requires it, for example to a regulator or a court, or to our
                    professional advisers where we need their advice.</p>

                <h2 class="h4 mt-5">Sending information outside the UK</h2>
                <p>Our live chat and our Dynamics 365 records are held in the United Kingdom, so no transfer is involved.</p>
                <p>Our website measurement is processed in the European Union, which the UK government has decided offers
                    adequate protection, so that transfer is permitted on that basis. Cloudflare serves this site from a
                    global network and may handle requests outside the UK and the EU. Where any of our suppliers processes
                    personal information outside a country covered by UK adequacy regulations, that transfer is governed by
                    the UK International Data Transfer Addendum to the European Commission's standard contractual clauses,
                    together with the supplier's own technical safeguards.</p>

                <h2 class="h4 mt-5">How long we keep it</h2>
                <div class="x4-cookie-table-wrap">
                    <table class="x4-cookie-table">
                        <caption class="visually-hidden">How long XFour keeps each kind of information</caption>
                        <thead>
                            <tr>
                                <th scope="col">What</th>
                                <th scope="col">How long</th>
                                <th scope="col">Why that long</th>
                            </tr>
                        </thead>
                        <tbody>
                            <tr>
                                <td>Live chat conversations and enquiries from people who do not become customers</td>
                                <td>24 months from your last contact with us, then deleted</td>
                                <td>Long enough to pick up a conversation that goes quiet and comes back, and to show what we
                                    were asked and what we said</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td>Records about customers</td>
                                <td>For as long as we work together, then 6 years</td>
                                <td>Six years is the period we may need to defend a legal claim and to meet our tax and
                                    accounting duties</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td>Website measurement</td>
                                <td>The daily identifier cannot be linked to you after the day it was made. The event records
                                    behind it are reviewed every 12 months and deleted once they are no longer useful</td>
                                <td>To compare one year with the next, and no longer</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td>Your cookie choice</td>
                                <td>12 months, then we ask you again</td>
                                <td>Consent should not last indefinitely</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td>Security and server logs</td>
                                <td>As set by Cloudflare, which is a short period measured in days</td>
                                <td>Investigating attacks and faults</td>
                            </tr>
                        </tbody>
                    </table>
                </div>

                <h2 class="h4 mt-5">Your rights</h2>
                <p>Under UK GDPR you can ask us to:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>Tell you what we hold</strong> about you, and give you a copy. This is a subject access
                        request.</li>
                    <li><strong>Correct</strong> anything that is wrong or incomplete.</li>
                    <li><strong>Delete</strong> what we hold, where we have no continuing reason to keep it.</li>
                    <li><strong>Restrict</strong> what we do with it while a question about it is being settled.</li>
                    <li><strong>Object</strong> to our use of it where we rely on legitimate interests — including our website
                        measurement, which you can stop yourself from <strong>Cookie choices</strong> in the footer.</li>
                    <li><strong>Receive it in a portable form</strong>, where we hold it with your consent or under a
                        contract.</li>
                    <li><strong>Withdraw consent</strong> you have given, at any time. For cookies, use
                        <strong>Cookie choices</strong> in the footer of any page.</li>
                </ul>
                <h3 class="h5 mt-4">How to exercise them</h3>
                <p>Email <a href="mailto:gdpr@xfour.co.uk">gdpr@xfour.co.uk</a>, or write to us at the registered office
                    above. Please tell us which right you want to use and enough detail for us to find your information. We
                    may need to check who you are first, so that we do not hand your information to someone else.</p>
                <p>It costs you nothing, and we will reply <strong>within one month</strong>. If your request is complicated
                    we may take up to two further months, and we will tell you within the first month if that happens.</p>

                <h2 class="h4 mt-5">If you are unhappy with us</h2>
                <p>Please tell us first at <a href="mailto:gdpr@xfour.co.uk">gdpr@xfour.co.uk</a>, so that we have the chance
                    to put it right.</p>
                <p>You also have the right to complain to the UK's data protection regulator, the Information Commissioner's
                    Office, at any time. You do not need our permission and you do not have to come to us first.</p>
                <ul>
                    <li><a href="https://ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint</a></li>
                    <li>Helpline 0303 123 1113</li>
                    <li>Information Commissioner's Office, Wycliffe House, Water Lane, Wilmslow, Cheshire, SK9 5AF</li>
                </ul>

                <h2 class="h4 mt-5">Cookies</h2>
                <p>Every cookie and browser storage item this site uses is named and explained in our
                    <a href="/legal/cookies">cookie policy</a>, including who sets it, what it is for and how long it lasts.
                    You can change your choices at any time:</p>
                <p>
                    <a class="btn btn-primary" role="button" href="/legal/cookies" data-x4-consent-open>Change your cookie choices</a>
                </p>

                <h2 class="h4 mt-5">Changes to this policy</h2>
                <p>If we change what we collect or why, we will update this page and change the date below before the change
                    takes effect. If the change is significant, and especially if it needs your consent, we will ask you again
                    rather than rely on an old answer.</p>

                <p class="text-muted mt-5"><small>Last updated 11 October 2026. This policy replaces our previous one-page
                    policy of 7 October 2026.</small></p>
            </article>
        </div>
    </section>
</BaseLayout>
